Subject: Pages asked for by a second instance open in the running window; a one-page run has one exit

Welcome Center is single-instance: a second start hands its arguments to the
running one, which raises its window. The pages a second start names with
--pages are shown in that window as layers over the pages it has open, so
Back returns to them and an entry that opens one page works while the tour
is open. A window that is itself a run of exactly those pages is only raised.
The update footer, which has only OK, gains a Back button while a layer is
open, so the Plasma update page under the layers stays reachable.

A --pages run of one page with no layer open shows neither Skip nor the page
indicator: Finish is its one exit.

